From: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: ls1021a-iot: add the FXOS8700CQ of the FRDM-KW41Z

The FRDM-KW41Z plugged in the Arduino headers carries the Bluetooth LE
controller of this setup and an FXOS8700CQ accelerometer and
magnetometer. The I2C lines of the Arduino headers (J8, J15) reach the
board I2C bus through the PCA9515 repeater (U10), which the CPLD keeps
enabled, so the sensor answers at 0x1f next to the board devices.

The FRDM-KW41Z is an add-on, not part of the board: this belongs in an
overlay upstream. Without it the probe fails and nothing else changes.

Signed-off-by: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/ls/ls1021a-iot.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/ls/ls1021a-iot.dts
@@ -216,6 +216,15 @@
 		reg = <0x51>;
 		read-only;
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Accelerometer and magnetometer of the FRDM-KW41Z on the Arduino
+	 * headers, behind the PCA9515 repeater (U10)
+	 */
+	magnetometer@1f {
+		compatible = "nxp,fxos8700";
+		reg = <0x1f>;
+	};
 };

 &lpuart0 {
